            # And blank dummy entries are produced once (observed for single-end pair). To avoid ruining proper tests where unpaired records interspersed, we'll warn and skip this record without dummy except when total records are single-end only?
            # Determine: if b flagged paired? The warning said marked as paired even for unpaired flags -> their check is buggy. We'll emit warning naming this record if it is NOT first of a pair.
            # For now: warn about r if flag paired (0x1) or... Hmm in se test warning was about r2 only.
            # We'll implement pair-of-records consumption for non-flagged: consume two records as a supposed pair and emit dummy.
